distance_calibration_savino,dataset,aeg-s-000343;aeg-s-000344;aeg-s-000345;aeg-s-000346;aeg-s-000347;aeg-s-000348;aeg-s-000349;aeg-s-000350;aeg-s-000351;aeg-s-000352;aeg-s-000354;aeg-s-000355;aeg-s-000357;aeg-s-000359;aeg-s-000360;aeg-s-000361;aeg-s-000362;aeg-s-000363;aeg-s-000364;aeg-s-000366;aeg-s-000375,both,given,0.035,,,fraction of D,,as_released,dw_distance,,not_published,"Savino et al. 2022, ApJ 938, 101",§7 l. 1244; §5 l. 952,"Savino §7 (Conclusions), l. 1244: ""Through extensive tests we quantified our typical systematic uncertainties to be ∼3.5%"". Possible overlap: Savino §5 (l. 952) says the quoted intervals ""have been computed to account for our uncertain knowledge of the RR Lyrae metallicity, pulsation parameters, and of the adopted PWZ calibration""; it does not say whether the 3.5 % overlaps them. Views show the term beside the error bars, never added in"
distance_calibration_other,dataset,*,both,not_given_by_source,,,,,,,dw_distance,,not_published,Carlin 2017; Higgs 2021; Medina 2018,l. 114; l. 361; l. 266,"Carlin et al. 2017's anchor modulus has no error (l. 114); Higgs et al. 2021's TRGB calibration states none (l. 361); Medina et al. 2018 (1802.01581v1, ms.tex, e-print SHA-256 3108c7bf…, l. 266) gives 1.8 % and ~3.6 % for assumed metallicity offsets of ±0.5 and ±1.0 dex, a conditional test, not an error"
velocity_error_model,dataset,*,g_obs,not_given_by_source,,,,,,,,,not_published,Geha 2026; Tollerud 2012; Heiger 2024; Kvasova 2024; Collins 2013,as in the note,"per-star floors inside each source's σ error; effect on σ not stated: Geha 2026 k_v 1.4, floor 1.1 km/s (l. 420); Tollerud 2012 2.2 km/s (l. 268); Heiger 2024 1 km/s (l. 109); Kvasova 2024 1.49 km/s (l. 260); Collins 2013 mask offsets (l. 571–573)"
binaries,system,*,g_obs,not_given_by_source,,,,,,,,,not_published,Wolf et al. 2010,l. 1212–1214,"Wolf l. 1212–1214: ""up to ∼20%"" in σ, only ""in the smallest dSphs"" (citing Minor 2010); rule 5. Screening per row in x_dwarfs_binary_screening (item 9)"
membership,system,*,g_obs,not_given_by_source,,,,,,,,,not_published,Tollerud et al. 2012,,"Tollerud's ""few-percent level"" applies to its own systems only (rule 5)"
