anisotropy_profile,dataset,*,g_obs,not_given_by_source,,,,,,,dw_equilibrium,,not_published,Wolf et al. 2010,l. 990–992,"Wolf l. 990–992: ""the errors on M_half increased by roughly 0.05 dex when the (rather extreme) second β(r) form was used"". This is the error of Wolf's own Jeans analysis, so rule 5 gives no size. The estimator-normalisation and anisotropy terms both describe the estimator; no source states their correlation"
